Title: One Cup
Credit: original short drama; names, events and dialogue are new
Author: Claude (draft)
Format: 6 scenes, 10 Flow generations of 4-9 s (one shot each), about 72 s, English dialogue
Tests: P17-01 stability run; a quiet two-hander in one room, props placed before the film starts and never handled

INT. BRENNAN KITCHEN - DAWN

[[look: small kitchen at dawn, square wooden table with two chairs, window behind the table with blue dawn light, warm pendant lamp above the table, a brass key and two white mugs on the table]]

HAL BRENNAN, seventies, sits at the kitchen table, a mug in front of him. His daughter IRIS BRENNAN, thirties, stands across the table in her coat. A brass key lies on the table in front of her.

HAL looks at the key, then up at her.

HAL
You could have posted it.

IRIS
I wanted to say goodbye, Dad. Properly.

INT. BRENNAN KITCHEN - DAWN

HAL
Where is it this time?

IRIS
Lisbon. A real job. I start Monday.

INT. BRENNAN KITCHEN - DAWN

HAL looks down at the key.

HAL
Your mother said that about Leeds.

IRIS
And she came back. I'm not her, Dad.

INT. BRENNAN KITCHEN - DAWN

HAL looks at the key for a long moment.

HAL
Keep the key. The lock never changed.

The key lies beside a second white mug, steam rising from it. He made her tea before she knocked.

INT. BRENNAN KITCHEN - DAWN

IRIS looks from the key to the steaming mug.

IRIS
You made me tea.

INT. BRENNAN KITCHEN - DAWN

IRIS sits down in the chair across from her father.

IRIS
One cup. Then I go.

HAL nods.
